silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_decomposition_step_2__step_typenegativewitness_=_typedleg_bot;_gate_refusetypedleg_bot_ a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The type operation assigns a NegativeWitness the bottom typed leg (TypedLeg_bot). The gate_refuse operation then converts TypedLeg_bot into the empty hom-set claim. This is different from a positive witness where type assigns a concrete TypedLeg and admit produces a typed leg for the cocone. A negative witness types as bot and the gate refuses, producing the empty hom-set assertion." .
